many of the stars of super bad were  launched to instant fame after the movie  became a giant hit but not all of them  were so lucky whatever happened to  Martha MacIsaac here's what she's been  up to and how she looks today  in 2011 MacIsaac took on the lead role  in hoax for the holidays a little-known  Canadian Christmas movie with an unusual  premise she plays a rebellious teen who  hoodwinked the residents of her small  town when she throws her coffee against  the wall of a donut store and  manipulates the stain so that it  resembles the face of Jesus Christ what  is it Jesus Christ for the Canadian  MacIsaac the film was very much a  homecoming and she had worked with a lot  of the same crew members on the CBC TV  series Emily of New Moon when she was a  kid in an interview with AXS she said  they were all like long-lost family to  get to come back and see all of them as  an adult was incredible in 2012 MacIsaac  went from playing a troublesome teen in  small-town Canada to playing a  troublesome teen in the White House she  was a main cast member in all 13  episodes of the NBC sitcom 1600 Penn as  the ordinarily straight-laced but  accidentally pregnant first daughter  Bill Pullman perhaps best known for  playing the president and the sci-fi  classic Independence Day once again took  on the role of commander-in-chief much  to the amusement of his co-stars  in an interview with she said media said  MacIsaac confirmed that Pullman could  handle the teasing saying he's one of  the nicest and down-to-earth men I've  ever had the pleasure of meeting he's  just one of those rare gems MacIsaac  scare achter also bore some coincidental  familiarity as she was named Becca just  like her super bad character sadly for  the actress her first full-time American  TV show didn't last very long it  suffered mediocre reviews and was axed  by NBC after a single season MacIsaac  married producer and director Tori  Catalano in 2010 but sadly their union  ended just five years later in that time  they worked together on a handful of  projects the first of which was a 2013  short named seasick sailor the two split  in 2015 the same year that catalano's  debut feature film almost anything later  renamed Milwaukee was really  it's a saucy dramedy about a bunch of  thirtysomethings testing the limits of  monogamy  it features MacIsaac as greta a woman  struggling with trust issues that  premise seems a little awkward now that  we know her marriage to Catalano was on  the rocks at the time post-divorce  MacIsaac has found a new man in her life  his name is Kyle McCullough and he's  dabbled in acting but he now appears to  be focused on working in the video game  industry in December 2018 the two had a  surprise wedding with none other than  Paul McCartney helping McCullagh out  with the proposal MacIsaac isn't  particularly close to any of the guys  from Superbad but she and Emma Stone  remain near and dear friends having even  spent a few years living together in  2012 MacIsaac presented her powell with  the first ever MTV Trailblazer award a  title that stone has more than lived up  to in the years since she got her first  Oscar nomination for 2014's Birdman and  then one a couple years later for lala  land and just like best friends should  be MacIsaac has been right by stone side  every step of the way and that has  proven herself as one of the most  enduring and captivating actresses of  our generation she's a gifted  entertainer and a very dear friend in  2017 MacIsaac joined fellow actresses  anna o'reilly and sugar lynn beard for a  pre oscars get together with all three  sporting t-shirts and support of stones  bid for Best Actress a couple of months  after the Oscar buzz had died down  Stoney MacIsaac went to a relaxing trip  to Sonoma in Northern California a  picturesque City located in the heart of  a world-renowned winemaking region Mac  Isaac's most recent major film role was  in 2017 sports biopic battle of the  sexes it's based on the true story of  the 1973 exhibition match between Billie  Jean King and Bobby Riggs a historic  moment in the history of women's tennis  King won in three straight sets meaning  Riggs who had belittled women's tennis  in the media had to eat his words  King was played by Emma Stone and her  bestie was right there alongside her  MacIsaac had the honor of plain-jane  peaches parka wits who is a member of  the original nine a group of female  players that included King and changed  tennis forever as it turns out the fact  that MacIsaac and stone are BFFs in real  life actually helped  and the wool co-director Valerie Faris  told cinema blend she and Emma are  friends and it just felt like if we  build this group of women that have a  certain camaraderie that can't hurt in  addition to battle of the sexes MacIsaac  has appeared in a couple of small  independent films the past few years  first up was unicorn store the  directorial debut of brie Larson  it features Larson as a woman who  receives a mysterious invitation to  fulfill her dreams the film also stars  samuel l.jackson Joan Cusack and Bradley  Whitford and it had its world premiere  at the 2017 Toronto International Film  Festival next up was the thriller what  keeps you alive which premiered at the  2018 South by Southwest festival it's  about a couple celebrating their first  anniversary at a remote cabin MacIsaac  plays a former childhood friend who  arouses suspicion when she shows up as  for the Future MacIsaac unfortunately  doesn't appear to have any film or TV  projects arriving any time soon but  judging by her Instagram she's been  keeping herself busy by baking delicious  looking cakes check out one of our  newest videos right here plus even more  looper videos about your favorite actors  and actresses are coming soon subscribe  to our YouTube channel and hit the bell  so you don't miss a single one  [Music]
 

